--- body ---
## Context
Execute agents routinely commit tickets/erg (the bootstrap binary) in feature
branches. Every subsequent CI rebuild on main then creates a binary conflict
on every rebase. The convention is: feature PRs touch only src/go/ and tests/;
CI's rebuild-binary.yml updates tickets/erg after merge in a dedicated commit.

A mechanical pre-commit hook enforces this more reliably than instructions.

## Actions
1. In the existing pre-commit hook (integration/hooks/pre-commit), add a check:
   if tickets/erg is in the staged files AND the current branch is not main,
   print an error and exit 1.
2. Error message:
   "pre-commit: do not commit tickets/erg in feature branches.
    CI rebuilds the binary after merge. Use 'make build' and test
    with build/erg. To override: git commit --no-verify"
3. Update integration.md to document the new check.

## Test
Stage tickets/erg on a non-main branch → commit must be rejected.
Stage tickets/erg on main → commit must succeed (CI rebuild commits).
Stage only .erg ticket files → commit must succeed (unrelated).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Pre-commit rejects `git add tickets/erg && git commit` on any non-main branch
- [ ] Pre-commit allows it on main (for CI rebuild commits)
- [ ] Error message names the correct remedy (make build, build/erg)
- [ ] integration.md documents the check
- [ ] make test passes
